TITLE:: PianoRoll
SUMMARY:: Piano-roll view for MIDI recording and note editing.
CATEGORIES:: Streams-Patterns-Events
RELATED:: Classes/PianoRollContainer, Classes/PianoRollNote, Classes/PianoRollPattern, Classes/PianoRollSidebar, Classes/PianoRollTimeline, Classes/PianoRollLoopMarkers, Classes/RealTimePlayer, Classes/Sequencer, Classes/SequencerGui, Classes/SequencerDocument, Classes/Metronome, Classes/SequencerKeyRouter, Classes/AddCommand, Classes/AmpCommand, Classes/DeleteCommand, Classes/DragCommand, Classes/LeftCommand, Classes/LegatoCommand, Classes/MidinoteCommand, Classes/PartCommand, Classes/RightCommand, Classes/SetCommand, Classes/SnapCommand, Classes/TransposeCommand, Classes/WriteCommand

DESCRIPTION::
LINK::Classes/PianoRoll:: is a LINK::Classes/SCViewHolder:: that shows recorded notes as a piano roll. Its root LINK::Classes/View:: uses a vertical layout: an embedded LINK::Classes/CommandPrompt:: at the top, a stretching horizontal layout below containing a LINK::Classes/ScrollView:: (timeline plus note canvas) and a fixed LINK::Classes/PianoRollSidebar:: on the right, and a transport strip along the bottom. That strip holds Start recording. Play loop and the Sync to menu (values 1 to 16, default 4) are shown only when the roll is not recording and contains at least one note. The sidebar shows the loop length from LINK::Classes/PianoRollLoopMarkers:: once both loop markers have been set, and, when exactly one note is selected, that note's CODE::midinote::, CODE::amp::, CODE::part:: (from LINK::Classes/PianoRollNote#-partNumber::), and any non-timing keys stored on its event. It embeds LINK::Classes/PianoRollTimeline:: for the beat strip above the roll (left/right clicks set loop bounds; Shift+left sets playback; see LINK::Classes/PianoRollTimeline::). LINK::#-receiveRecordingMidi:: draws a LINK::Classes/PianoRollNote:: as a LINK::Classes/BorderView:: when its note-off inserts it into the roll. Part numbers wrap across LINK::Classes/GuiPalette#-colour1::, LINK::Classes/GuiPalette#-colour2::, LINK::Classes/GuiPalette#-colour3::, LINK::Classes/GuiPalette#-colour4::, and LINK::Classes/GuiPalette#-colour5::. Part 5 uses colour5. Part 6 uses colour1. Part 9 uses colour4. An unselected note's border is that colour at full opacity. A selected note's border is LINK::Classes/GuiPalette#-extreme2::. The fill is the same colour at an opacity equal to the note's amplitude. Until CODE::\amp:: is written, that amplitude is the MIDI velocity mapped from 0–127 onto 0–1. LINK::Classes/AmpCommand:: sets CODE::\amp:: and the fill opacity follows it. LINK::#-startRecording:: and LINK::#-stopRecording:: announce CODE::\isRecording:: to dependants. LINK::#-stopRecording:: announces CODE::false:: before it finalizes the take, then updates LINK::Classes/PianoRollLoopMarkers:: from recorded notes. Keystrokes on the note area are reported to the LINK::Classes/SequencerKeyRouter:: passed in at construction.

SUBSECTION:: Keyboard editing
Focus the note area after clicking it:

TABLE::
## Keys || Behaviour
## 1–9 || Assign part on selected notes
## Ctrl+Z || Undo the last recorded command
## Ctrl+Shift+Z, Ctrl+Y || Redo
## Delete || Delete the selected notes
## Escape || Focus the command prompt
::

Edits update the embedded LINK::Classes/RealTimePlayer:: sequence and are allowed during playback. LINK::#-startRecording:: starts the LINK::Classes/Metronome::; LINK::#-stopRecording:: stops it. Note operations such as amp, delete, left, legato, midinote, part, right, set, snap, transpose, and write are invoked through the embedded LINK::Classes/CommandPrompt::. The prompt is constructed with LINK::Classes/AmpCommand#*new::, LINK::Classes/DeleteCommand#*new::, LINK::Classes/LeftCommand#*new::, LINK::Classes/LegatoCommand#*new::, LINK::Classes/MidinoteCommand#*new::, LINK::Classes/PartCommand#*new::, LINK::Classes/RightCommand#*new::, LINK::Classes/SetCommand#*new:: (passing LINK::Classes/AmpCommand::, LINK::Classes/LegatoCommand::, LINK::Classes/MidinoteCommand::, and LINK::Classes/PartCommand::), LINK::Classes/SnapCommand#*new::, LINK::Classes/TransposeCommand#*new::, and LINK::Classes/WriteCommand#*new:: (passing the optional LINK::Classes/SequencerDocument:: and this roll's LINK::Classes/Sequencer::). Ambient parameters supply CODE::selectedNotes::, CODE::allNotes::, CODE::loopStart::, CODE::loopEnd::, and CODE::midiChannel::. CODE::loopStart:: and CODE::loopEnd:: are nil until both loop markers have been set. The CODE::delete:: command removes every selected note from the roll and from the sequence. The CODE::left:: and CODE::right:: commands move every selected note by the typed CODE::resolution::. The CODE::transpose:: command adds the typed integer to every selected note's MIDI note number. The CODE::write:: command inserts a CODE::Seq().addMidiSequence:: line via LINK::Classes/SequencerDocument#-insertPattern::.

SUBSECTION:: Navigation
The mouse wheel scrolls the roll vertically. Shift and the mouse wheel scroll it horizontally; wheel-up moves toward earlier beats. Ctrl and the mouse wheel zoom horizontally through four steps: half, the default scale, double, and quadruple. Wheel-up zooms in. The beat under the pointer stays put. The canvas is 130 beats wide. LINK::#-loadPattern:: grows that count when the loaded phrase runs past it, and later zoom uses the grown count. Recording does not grow the canvas. Dragging a note moves its start time in steps of a quarter beat and its MIDI number by whole steps. The note view jumps to those positions while the button is held. A note that did not start on a quarter snaps to the nearest one once the pointer has moved. Releasing the button records one LINK::Classes/DragCommand:: step for that note's onset, stop time, and MIDI note number. Movement while the button is held is not recorded. A release that leaves the note where it was records nothing. Dragging on empty roll space draws a rectangle and selects the notes inside it. Clicking a note selects that note. Without Ctrl, a click or an empty-space drag clears the previous selection first. Ctrl+drag on empty space and Ctrl+click add to the selection. Ctrl+click does not move the note. Clicking empty space clears the selection unless Ctrl is held.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates a LINK::Classes/PianoRoll::.

ARGUMENT:: parent
Unused in the current implementation; reserved for embedding.

ARGUMENT:: bounds
Unused in the current implementation; reserved for layout.

ARGUMENT:: palette
A LINK::Classes/GuiPalette:: used for colours.

ARGUMENT:: sequencer
The LINK::Classes/Sequencer:: whose shared playback clock this roll uses for playback and recording.

ARGUMENT:: devMode
When true, skips MIDI and server setup.

ARGUMENT:: keyRouter
The LINK::Classes/SequencerKeyRouter:: used for Record-view keyboard shortcuts.

ARGUMENT:: sequencerDocument
An optional LINK::Classes/SequencerDocument:: used to write pattern source. Pass CODE::nil:: when embedding without a document.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: assignSelectedToPart
Sets the part of every selected note by executing LINK::Classes/PartCommand::. CODE::partNumber:: is an integer from 1 to 9.

ARGUMENT:: partNumber
The part to assign. An integer from 1 to 9.

METHOD:: commandPrompt
The embedded LINK::Classes/CommandPrompt:: instance used for command input.

RETURNS::
A LINK::Classes/CommandPrompt::.

METHOD:: deleteSelected
Deletes every selected note by executing LINK::Classes/DeleteCommand::. An empty selection does nothing.

METHOD:: focusBackground
Gives keyboard focus to the note area.

METHOD:: loadPattern
Places CODE::pattern:: on this roll. Each note is shifted by four beats, so the phrase starts at time 4. Counting the left edge as beat 1, that is beat 5. A leading rest stays inside the phrase, after that margin. The loop starts at time 4 and ends at time 4 plus LINK::Classes/PianoRollPattern#-duration::, which includes the final step's CODE::\dur::. The playhead is put on the loop start. A zero duration leaves the loop unset. The end is not snapped to a quarter beat and is not clipped to 130 beats. Notes are inserted directly, with no undo step. The canvas grows when the loop end or a note stop is past 130 beats. Playback uses CODE::midiChannel::. When every note carries the same numeric CODE::\chan::, that channel is used instead.

ARGUMENT:: pattern
A LINK::Classes/PianoRollPattern::.

ARGUMENT:: midiChannel
The MIDI channel for playback, or CODE::nil:: to leave the roll's channel unchanged unless the pattern supplies one. The arranger passes the sequence synth's channel.

METHOD:: playLoop
Starts playback of the recorded sequence. The embedded LINK::Classes/RealTimePlayer:: acquires the sequencer's shared clock and releases that hold when playback stops. When this play creates the clock, that clock is set to beat 0. The playhead then snaps to the nearest point on the LINK::#-syncTo:: grid that shares the clock's offset into that grid, measured from the loop start around the loop, and playback starts from there immediately. Returns false and posts a warning if no notes have been recorded.

METHOD:: receiveRecordingMidi
Records one MIDI message into the open take. A note-on creates a LINK::Classes/PianoRollNote:: and holds it until the matching note-off. A note-off sets that note's stop time and inserts it into the roll as one undo step. Does nothing when this roll is not recording.

ARGUMENT:: msgType
CODE::\noteOn:: or CODE::\noteOff::.

ARGUMENT:: velocity
The note-on velocity.

ARGUMENT:: noteNumber
The MIDI note number.

ARGUMENT:: chan
The MIDI channel. A note-on stores it on the embedded LINK::Classes/RealTimePlayer::.

METHOD:: redo
Restores the most recently undone command on this roll. Does nothing when there is nothing to redo, including when no command has recorded an undo step yet.

METHOD:: selectedNotes
Returns an LINK::Classes/Array:: of currently selected LINK::Classes/PianoRollNote:: instances.

RETURNS::
An LINK::Classes/Array:: of LINK::Classes/PianoRollNote:: instances.

METHOD:: startRecording
Acquires the sequencer's shared clock, creating it at beat 0 when nothing else holds it, and timestamps notes from that clock. Starts the LINK::Classes/Metronome:: on that same clock, then announces CODE::\isRecording:: as CODE::true:: to dependants. Does nothing if recording is already in progress.

METHOD:: stopLoop
Stops playback via the embedded LINK::Classes/RealTimePlayer::. That player releases its hold on the shared clock after the final slice sends note-offs. Does nothing when playback is not in progress.

METHOD:: stopRecording
Announces CODE::\isRecording:: as CODE::false:: to dependants, stops the LINK::Classes/Metronome::, drops any note still held with no note-off, updates LINK::Classes/PianoRollLoopMarkers:: from recorded notes (loop bounds plus LINK::Classes/PianoRollLoopMarkers#-playheadTime_:: at the loop start beat), and releases this roll's hold on the shared clock. Does nothing when recording is not in progress.

METHOD:: syncTo
The Sync-to grid in beats. An integer from 1 to 16. The default is 4. LINK::#-playLoop:: uses it to choose where the playhead starts.

ARGUMENT:: newSyncTo
The new grid size when setting. An integer from 1 to 16.

METHOD:: undo
Restores the previous recorded command on this roll. Does nothing when the undo stack is empty. A command records a step only when its LINK::Classes/Command#-beforeImage:: is a non-empty dictionary. Ctrl+Z calls this when the note area is focused.

PRIVATE:: init, prApplyNoteEdits, prColourForPart, prDeleteNote, prEnsureBeats, prExecuteCommand, prFillForNote, prInsertNote, prMakeTransportStrip, prPaintNote, prPlaceLoadedNote, prRefreshSidebar, prSelectedNotes, prUpdateLoopControls
